been out on a shift with one of our  refuse crews today collecting black bins  across shilland and higham it's been a  great opportunity to chat to the team  and experience what they do every day  first hand we've been quite lucky with  the rain today but the crews are out in  all weathers and it's hard work even  just lining up the bins right on the  lifter  thank you to the guys for being so  welcoming and patient but equally thank  you to all our street team staff for  what they do for us day in Day Out  I've just got back home after a day with  one of our refuse Crews we've been been  around dronfield and unston and  cutthorpe today it's been fantastic to  do it I've really enjoyed myself it's  been absolutely torrential rain all day  so I'm thoroughly drenched now but it's  been fantastic to see how hard our  refuse Crews work across the district  and spend a bit more time and learn  about some of the challenges that they  face and what it's like to actually to  actually do the role and so the spender  uh you know walk a mile in their shoes  as it were and it's been really  heartening to see actually how many of  our residents appreciate what they're  doing by giving them small gifts like  bottles of water and and lovely things  like that so it's really great to see I  really enjoyed it and I want to say a  big thank you to all of our refuse Crews  across the district council they do a  fantastic job day in day out and in  particular I want to thank Dave Lloyd  and Adam who were really welcoming and  showed me showed me all the ropes and  and really looked after me very well so  big thank you to everyone I had a great  time and I'm sure I'll be doing it again  before too long
 

